      en: "Augusta Raurica is the oldest Roman colonial city in Switzerland, founded around 44 BC near Augst. The excavation site covers 70 hectares and includes a well-preserved theater with 8,000 seats, a temple district, and a basilica. The Roman Museum displays finds such as the Kaiseraugst silver treasure. The city wall was 4 kilometers long. Augusta Raurica was a major trade and administrative center. Over 100,000 people visit the site annually. The theater is used for concerts today. The settlement was inhabited until the 4th century.",
